{
  "id": "honest-signal",
  "term": "honest signal",
  "definition": "An honest signal is a cue or display that reliably gives a receiver true information about some aspect of the signaller’s quality or condition. In this context, different signals may each be honest about different features or time scales, and several signals together can convey more complete information than one alone.",
